# WorldSim v5 environment variables
# Copy to .env and fill in.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLAUDE AUTH — pick ONE of the three methods below
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by both (a) Claude Code inside Modal sandboxes (planning, profiling,
# ecological-validity probe, placement-fix, ecoval-fix) and (b) the host-side
# Anthropic Messages API calls for the Phase 4 judge and variant generator
# (see worldsim/phase_4/{judge_api,variant_api}.py, as of 2026-04-18).
#
# Three auth paths, in priority order (see worldsim/modal_sandbox.py:_build_claude_secrets
# and worldsim/phase_4/anthropic_client.py):
#
# 1) CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN — Claude Pro / Max subscription auth (preferred).
#    Cheapest per call. Works with BOTH the Modal sandbox AND the host Messages
#    API (via Authorization: Bearer header; see phase_2_text_fill._call_anthropic_fallback).
#    If set, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL are NOT forwarded into
#    sandbox — OAuth doesn't route through a proxy.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=your_oauth_token_here
#
# 2) ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN + ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL — OpenRouter (or any proxy).
#    Put your OpenRouter key in ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (not ANTHROPIC_API_KEY),
#    set the base URL to https://openrouter.ai/api (no /v1 suffix), and leave
#    ANTHROPIC_API_KEY empty. Sandbox handles blanking ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#    automatically when ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN is set.
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=sk-or-v1-...
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
#
# 3) ANTHROPIC_API_KEY alone — direct Anthropic API, billed per token.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here
#
# If CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is set alongside ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OAuth wins.
# Empty strings (e.g., ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="") are treated as unset by the host
# API path, matching the sandbox convention.
#
# GOTCHA — split credit pool between OPENROUTER_API_KEY and ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN:
#   If your funded OpenRouter credit lives under OPENROUTER_API_KEY (the key
#   Browser-Use reads, below) but ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN is set to a DIFFERENT
#   (possibly depleted) OpenRouter token, the auth precedence above will pick
#   ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN and the Phase 4 judge/variant API calls will 402.
#   Three ways to fix:
#     (a) Alias the funded key before running:
#           export ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN="$OPENROUTER_API_KEY"
#     (b) Top up the ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN token's credits.
#     (c) Clear ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (and ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL) so OAuth or
#         ANTHROPIC_API_KEY takes over.
#   Phase 4 now pre-flights the API before running any task — a bad credential
#   fails at startup cost ~$0.0001 instead of after Browser-Use burns eval cost.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODAL AUTHENTICATION
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How YOU authenticate against Modal to create sandboxes. Easiest path:
# `modal token new` — writes ~/.modal.toml. For CI/containers, set these:
# MODAL_TOKEN_ID=ak-...
# MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET=as-...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODAL NAMED-SECRET OVERRIDE (opt-in, CI-friendly)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you have a curated Modal secret in a shared workspace, set its name
# here and worldsim will use Secret.from_name(<value>) instead of packaging
# your local shell env vars. The OAuth-wins fixup above does NOT apply in
# this mode — whatever env vars the named secret contains are injected
# as-is, so managing them is your responsibility.
#
# Create one with e.g.:
#   modal secret create my-claude-secret CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=claude-...
#
# Then:
# WORLDSIM_CLAUDE_MODAL_SECRET=my-claude-secret

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BROWSER USE — evaluation agent LLM (Phases 3 and 4)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser Use runs LOCALLY (not in Modal). Its LLM provider is configured
# via the `llm` param in BrowserUseAgent (see worldsim/main.py).
# These keys are LOCAL-ONLY — NOT forwarded into Modal sandboxes.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEBARENA BENCHMARK INSTANCES (Phases 3 and 4)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The user stands up WebArena instances per the v5 spec "Prerequisites" section
# and supplies them to the orchestrator via worldsim/main.py configuration.
# These placeholders are just a convenience for editing main.py / instances.json.
# Phase 3/4 HTTP-form seeding currently expects these auth headers when you seed
# storefront/customer content directly:
# WORLDSIM_SHOPPING_AUTO_LOGIN=emma.lopez@gmail.com:Password.123
# WORLDSIM_REDDIT_AUTO_LOGIN=MarvelsGrantMan136:test1234
#
# Shopping Admin seeding auth stays config-driven, not env-driven. Its instance
# config should include a static header like:
#   "auth": {
#     "type": "http_headers",
#     "headers": {
#       "X-M2-Admin-Auto-Login": "admin:admin1234"
#     }
#   }
#
# Keep db_connection concrete in instances.json. Do not use env interpolation
# for DB URIs. Typical WebArena Verified examples:
# - shopping / shopping_admin: mysql://magentouser:MyPassword@HOST:3306/magentodb
# - reddit: postgresql://postmill:postmill@HOST:5432/postmill
# - map: postgresql://openstreetmap:openstreetmap@HOST:5433/openstreetmap
# WORLDSIM_WEBARENA_SHOPPING_URL=http://localhost:7770
# WORLDSIM_WEBARENA_SHOPPING_DB=mysql://user:pass@localhost:3306/opencart
# WORLDSIM_WEBARENA_SHOPPING_RESET=http://localhost:7770/reset

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Override where pipeline state and artifacts are written (default: ./logs/).
# WORLDSIM_STATE_DIR=logs
